faith or other\nconstraint on the business's discretion. The provision is material, and its effect is to render\nthe contract illusory. The court should give deference to the consumer's choice whether to\nsever the provision and enforce the remainder of the contract or treat the entire contract as\nunenforceable.\n3. Gap-filling. When the court decides to enforce the contract without the offending term,\nthe court may be required to fill a gap left by the unenforceable term. For example, if a price term\nis excessive and unconscionable, or if a period of limitations is too short and unconscionable, the\n166\n@ 10\n"